RANK()

  ASSIGNS RANK WITH GAPE


  EX:

EX:ASSIGN RANK WITH GAPE NOT DEPT WISE(NO PARTITION BY)

select emp.*,RANK() OVER( ORDER BY SAL DESc) as rn
from emp;


EX:ASSIGN RANK WITH GAP FROM EACH DEPT WISE(USE PARTITION BY)

select emp.*,RANKR() OVER(PARTITION BY DEPTNO ORDER BY SAL DESc) as rn
from emp;


Rank Employees by Salary.
  
SELECT ENAME,SAL,RANK() OVER(ORDER BY SAL DESC) RN
FROM EMP;

Output
ENAME	SAL	RN
KING	5000	1
SCOTT	3000	2
FORD	3000	2
JONES	2975	4

AJS Rank skips numbers after ties.

DENSE_RANK()
SELECT ENAME,SAL,
       DENSE_RANK() OVER(ORDER BY SAL DESC) RN
FROM EMP;
Output
ENAME	SAL	RN
KING	5000	1
SCOTT	3000	2
FORD	3000	2
JONES	2975	3

✅ No rank gaps.

Top 3 Salaries using DENSE_RANK
SELECT *
FROM(
    SELECT ENAME,SAL,
           DENSE_RANK() OVER(ORDER BY SAL DESC) RN
    FROM EMP
)
WHERE RN<=3;
Output
ENAME	SAL	RN
KING	5000	1
SCOTT	3000	2
FORD	3000	2
JONES	2975	3
